lisa-design:
- opencode registers a skill by its SKILL.md front-matter `name`, not its folder (packages/opencode/src/skill/index.ts at v1.19.6: `state.skills[md.data.name]`, loaded concurrently, a duplicate overwrites). Names may contain `:` there (no validation); the problem is only that opencode has no plugin namespace.
- So a clash copy (<plugin>-<name>/) gets `name: <plugin>-<name>` in its copied SKILL.md (clirun.setSkillName), else the instructions' `ccf-review:review → ccf-review-review` would name a skill opencode doesn't have. Done in the shared clirun copy: codex's clash copies get it too (harmless whether codex keys by folder or by name). Only when folder != name; non-clash copies are byte-for-byte.
- Not taken: registering skills as `<plugin>:<skill>` in the copies, because prompts also name plain skills (`docs-style`) and the catalog's `use:` lists mix both forms.
- clirun.FlatSkills is the one naming rule; flattenSkills uses it, opencode's instructions list it. Codex's AGENTS.md is unchanged (spec: no evidence it needs it).

